#: include/global_settings.php:436
msgid "Graph Permission Method"
msgstr "Paraan ng Graph Permission"

#: include/global_settings.php:437
msgid "There are four methods for determining a User's Graph Permissions.  The first is 'Permissive'.  Under the 'Permissive' setting, a User only needs access to either the Graph, Device or Graph Template to gain access to the Graphs that apply to them.  Under 'Restrictive', the User must have access to the Graph, the Device, and the Graph Template to gain access to the Graph.  These first two methods have scalability problems for very large installs.  So, two additional options are available.  They are 'Device Based', which means if you have access to the Device, you get access to it's Graphs.  And lastly 'Graph Template Based', which means if you have access to the 'Graph Template' you get access to all Device Graphs of that Template."
msgstr "May apat na paraan upang tukuyin ang Mga Pahintulot sa Graph ng isang User.  Ang una ay 'Permissive'.  Sa setting na 'Permissive', kailangan lamang ng User ng access sa Graph, Device o Graph Template upang makakuha ng access sa mga Graph na naaangkop sa kanya.  Sa 'Restrictive', dapat may access ang User sa Graph, sa Device, at sa Graph Template upang makakuha ng access sa Graph.  May problema sa scalability ang unang dalawang paraang ito sa napakalalaking install.  Kaya, may dalawa pang opsyon.  Ang mga ito ay 'Device Based', na nangangahulugang kung may access ka sa Device, may access ka sa mga Graph nito.  At panghuli ang 'Graph Template Based', na nangangahulugang kung may access ka sa 'Graph Template' ay may access ka sa lahat ng Graph ng Device ng Template na iyon."

#: include/global_settings.php:441
msgid "Permissive"
msgstr "Maluwag"

#: include/global_settings.php:442
msgid "Restrictive"
msgstr "Mahigpit"

#: include/global_settings.php:443
msgid "Device Based"
msgstr "Batay sa Device"

#: include/global_settings.php:449
msgid "Graph/Data Source Creation Method"
msgstr "Paraan ng Paglikha ng Graph/Data Source"

#: include/global_settings.php:450
msgid "If set to Simple, Graphs and Data Sources can only be created from New Graphs.  If Advanced, legacy Graph and Data Source creation is supported."
msgstr "Kung nakatakda sa Simple, ang mga Graph at Data Source ay malilikha lamang mula sa New Graphs.  Kung Advanced, suportado ang legacy na paglikha ng Graph at Data Source."

#: include/global_settings.php:453
msgid "Simple"
msgstr "Payak"

#: include/global_settings.php:454 lib/html.php:2949
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr "Masulong"

#: include/global_settings.php:458
msgid "Show Form/Setting Help Inline"
msgstr "Ipakita ang Tulong ng Form/Setting nang Inline"

#: include/global_settings.php:459
msgid "When checked, Form and Setting Help will be show inline.  Otherwise it will be presented when hovering over the help button."
msgstr "Kapag may check, ipapakita nang inline ang Tulong sa Form at Setting.  Kung hindi, ipapakita ito kapag itinapat ang cursor sa help button."

#: include/global_settings.php:464
msgid "Local Page Help Only"
msgstr "Local na Tulong sa Pahina Lamang"

#: include/global_settings.php:465
msgid "By default Cacti page help is located at docs.cacti.net.  However, if your system does not have access to the Internet, you may download the documentation locally in HTML format and host it in the 'docs' location of you Cacti server.  If you choose only to leverage the local location for page help documentation, check this checkbox."
msgstr "Bilang default, ang page help ng Cacti ay nasa docs.cacti.net.  Gayunpaman, kung walang access sa Internet ang iyong system, maaari mong i-download ang dokumentasyon nang lokal sa HTML format at i-host ito sa lokasyong 'docs' ng iyong Cacti server.  Kung nais mong gamitin lamang ang lokal na lokasyon para sa dokumentasyon ng page help, lagyan ng check ang checkbox na ito."

#: include/global_settings.php:470
msgid "Deletion Verification"
msgstr "Pagpapatunay ng Pagbura"

#: include/global_settings.php:471
msgid "Prompt user before item deletion."
msgstr "Tanungin ang user bago burahin ang item."

#: include/global_settings.php:476
msgid "Data Source Preservation Preset"
msgstr "Preset ng Pag-iingat ng Data Source"

#: include/global_settings.php:477
msgid "When enabled, Cacti will set Radio Button to Delete related Data Sources of a Graph when removing Graphs.  Note: Cacti will not allow the removal of Data Sources if they are used in other Graphs."
msgstr "Kapag naka-enable, itatakda ng Cacti ang Radio Button upang Burahin ang mga kaugnay na Data Source ng isang Graph kapag nag-aalis ng mga Graph.  Tandaan: Hindi papayagan ng Cacti ang pag-alis ng mga Data Source kung ginagamit ang mga ito sa ibang mga Graph."

#: include/global_settings.php:482
msgid "Graphs Auto Unlock"
msgstr "Awtomatikong Pag-unlock ng mga Graph"

#: include/global_settings.php:483
msgid "When enabled, Cacti will not lock Graphs.  This allow a faster manual modification of Data Sources related to a Graph."
msgstr "Kapag naka-enable, hindi ila-lock ng Cacti ang mga Graph.  Pinapabilis nito ang manu-manong pagbabago ng mga Data Source na kaugnay ng isang Graph."

#: include/global_settings.php:488
msgid "Hide Cacti Dashboard"
msgstr "Itago ang Cacti Dashboard"

#: include/global_settings.php:489
msgid "For use with Cacti's External Link Support.  Using this setting, you can hide the Cacti Dashboard, so you can display just your own page."
msgstr "Para sa paggamit sa External Link Support ng Cacti.  Gamit ang setting na ito, maaari mong itago ang Cacti Dashboard, upang ang sarili mong page lamang ang maipakita."

#: include/global_settings.php:494
msgid "Enable Drag-N-Drop"
msgstr "I-enable ang Drag-N-Drop"

#: include/global_settings.php:495
msgid "Some of Cacti's interfaces support Drag-N-Drop.  If checked this option will be enabled.  Note: For visually impaired user, this option may be disabled."
msgstr "Sinusuportahan ng ilang interface ng Cacti ang Drag-N-Drop.  Kapag may check, ie-enable ang opsyong ito.  Tandaan: Para sa mga user na may kapansanan sa paningin, maaaring i-disable ang opsyong ito."

#: include/global_settings.php:500
msgid "Site Security"
msgstr "Seguridad ng Site"

#: include/global_settings.php:505
msgid "Force Connections over HTTPS"
msgstr "Pilitin ang mga Koneksyon sa HTTPS"

#: include/global_settings.php:506
msgid "When checked, any attempts to access Cacti will be redirected to HTTPS to ensure high security."
msgstr "Kapag may check, ang anumang pagtatangkang mag-access sa Cacti ay ire-redirect sa HTTPS upang matiyak ang mataas na seguridad."

#: include/global_settings.php:511
msgid "Allow Unsafe Remote Data Collector HTTPS"
msgstr "Payagan ang Hindi Ligtas na HTTPS ng Remote Data Collector"

#: include/global_settings.php:512
msgid "Allow the use of Self Signed Certificates and allow the hostname of the Certificate to differ from that of the Remote Data Collector."
msgstr "Payagan ang paggamit ng Self Signed Certificate at payagang magkaiba ang hostname ng Certificate sa hostname ng Remote Data Collector."

#: include/global_settings.php:517
msgid "Allow Unsafe Metacharacters in Data Input Methods"
msgstr "Payagan ang Hindi Ligtas na Metacharacter sa mga Data Input Method"

#: include/global_settings.php:518
msgid "Historically, Cacti administrators created simple Data Input Methods that include commands like \"ps -ef | grep something | wc -l\" to represent a numeric value for use in Cacti Graphs.  In earlier versions of Cacti, this was permitted.  However, this is an unsafe practice as it is a gateway for third party users to publish insecure Data Templates.  In modern Cacti, these types of practices should be avoided.  However, we provide this option if you have older Data Input Methods that contain these unsafe Meta Characters and have not converted them to local scripts in the 'scripts' directory.  When this option is unchecked, Cacti restricts shell-style metacharacters such as quotation marks, curly brackets, vertical bars, backslashes, and backticks.  Cacti continues to allow greater-than and less-than signs for things like <path_cacti> and for input parameters, but if this option is unchecked, that is the limit of their permitted use."
msgstr "Noon, gumawa ang mga Cacti administrator ng mga simpleng Data Input Method na may mga command gaya ng \"ps -ef | grep something | wc -l\" upang kumatawan sa numerong halaga para magamit sa mga Cacti Graph.  Sa mga naunang bersyon ng Cacti, pinapayagan ito.  Gayunpaman, hindi ligtas na gawain ito dahil nagiging daan ito para makapaglathala ang mga third party user ng mga hindi ligtas na Data Template.  Sa makabagong Cacti, dapat iwasan ang ganitong mga gawain.  Gayunpaman, ibinibigay namin ang opsyong ito kung mayroon kang mas lumang Data Input Method na may mga hindi ligtas na Meta Character na ito at hindi mo pa nako-convert ang mga ito sa mga lokal na script sa 'scripts' directory.  Kapag walang check ang opsyong ito, nililimitahan ng Cacti ang mga shell-style na metacharacter gaya ng quotation mark, curly bracket, vertical bar, backslash, at backtick.  Patuloy na pinapayagan ng Cacti ang mga simbolong greater-than at less-than para sa mga bagay gaya ng <path_cacti> at para sa mga input parameter, ngunit kung walang check ang opsyong ito, iyon na ang hangganan ng pinapayagang paggamit ng mga ito."

#: include/global_settings.php:524
msgid "Content-Security Script Policy"
msgstr "Patakaran sa Script ng Content-Security"

#: include/global_settings.php:525
msgid "Controls the script-src CSP policy.  In Nonce Modes, Cacti Plugins that use inline JavaScript must include the nonce attribute from Cacti's builtin function 'CactiSecureHeaders::getNonceAttribute()'. Otherwise, those scripts will be blocked by the browser.  Currently, Cacti only allows reporting on Cacti Plugins that do not properly use Nonce Mode.  In the future, we will allow Administrators to block such plugins from using their inline JavaScript if they are not using Nonces."
msgstr "Kinokontrol ang script-src CSP policy.  Sa Nonce Mode, ang mga Cacti Plugin na gumagamit ng inline JavaScript ay dapat magsama ng nonce attribute mula sa builtin function ng Cacti na 'CactiSecureHeaders::getNonceAttribute()'. Kung hindi, haharangin ng browser ang mga script na iyon.  Sa kasalukuyan, pinapayagan lamang ng Cacti ang pag-uulat sa mga Cacti Plugin na hindi wastong gumagamit ng Nonce Mode.  Sa hinaharap, papayagan namin ang mga Administrator na harangin ang mga naturang plugin sa paggamit ng kanilang inline JavaScript kung hindi sila gumagamit ng mga Nonce."

#: include/global_settings.php:528
msgid "Allow Non-Nonced Inline JavaScript"
msgstr "Payagan ang Non-Nonced Inline JavaScript"

#: include/global_settings.php:529
msgid "Allow both unsafe-eval and Non-Nonced Inline JavaScript"
msgstr "Payagan ang parehong unsafe-eval at Non-Nonced Inline JavaScript"

#: include/global_settings.php:530
msgid "Nonce Mode - Reporting Only"
msgstr "Nonce Mode - Pag-uulat Lamang"

#: include/global_settings.php:534 include/global_settings.php:549
msgid "CSP Violation Report URI"
msgstr "URI ng Ulat ng Paglabag sa CSP"

#: include/global_settings.php:535
msgid "URL where browsers POST CSP violation reports in nonce-report and nonce modes. Leave empty to use <url_path>/csp_report.php. Must contain only safe URL characters."
msgstr "URL kung saan nagpo-POST ang mga browser ng mga CSP violation report sa mga mode na nonce-report at nonce. Iwanang walang laman upang gamitin ang <url_path>/csp_report.php. Dapat maglaman lamang ng mga ligtas na URL character."

#: include/global_settings.php:541
msgid "Content-Security Alternate Sources"
msgstr "Mga Alternatibong Pinagmulan ng Content-Security"

#: include/global_settings.php:542
msgid "Space delimited domain names that will be permitted to be accessed outside of the Web Server itself.  This is important for users choosing to use a CDN, or hosting site.  Sources can includes wildcards for example: *.mydomain.com, or a protocol, for example: https://*.example.com.  These Alternate Sources include Image, CSS and JavaScript types only."
msgstr "Mga domain name na pinaghihiwalay ng espasyo na papayagang ma-access sa labas ng Web Server mismo.  Mahalaga ito para sa mga user na pumipiling gumamit ng CDN, o hosting site.  Maaaring magsama ang mga Source ng mga wildcard halimbawa: *.mydomain.com, o isang protocol, halimbawa: https://*.example.com.  Ang mga Alternatibong Source na ito ay para lamang sa Image, CSS at JavaScript."

#: include/global_settings.php:550
msgid "URL where browsers POST CSP violation reports in nonce-report and nonce modes. Leave empty to use /cacti/csp_report.php at the installation root. Must contain only safe URL characters."
msgstr "URL kung saan nagpo-POST ang mga browser ng mga CSP violation report sa mga mode na nonce-report at nonce. Iwanang walang laman upang gamitin ang /cacti/csp_report.php sa installation root. Dapat maglaman lamang ng mga ligtas na URL character."

#: include/global_settings.php:562
msgid "Enable Automatic Graph Creation"
msgstr "I-enable ang Awtomatikong Paglikha ng Graph"

#: include/global_settings.php:563
msgid "When disabled, Cacti Automation will not actively create any Graph.  This is useful when adjusting Device settings so as to avoid creating new Graphs each time you save an object.  Invoking Automation Rules manually will still be possible."
msgstr "Kapag naka-disable, hindi aktibong gagawa ng anumang Graph ang Cacti Automation.  Kapaki-pakinabang ito sa pag-aayos ng mga setting ng Device upang maiwasang lumikha ng mga bagong Graph tuwing magse-save ng object.  Posible pa ring manu-manong gamitin ang mga Automation Rule."

#: include/global_settings.php:568
msgid "Enable Automatic Tree Item Creation"
msgstr "I-enable ang Awtomatikong Paglikha ng Tree Item"

#: include/global_settings.php:569
msgid "When disabled, Cacti Automation will not actively create any Tree Item.  This is useful when adjusting Device or Graph settings so as to avoid creating new Tree Entries each time you save an object.  Invoking Rules manually will still be possible."
msgstr "Kapag naka-disable, hindi aktibong gagawa ng anumang Tree Item ang Cacti Automation.  Kapaki-pakinabang ito sa pag-aayos ng mga setting ng Device o Graph upang maiwasang lumikha ng mga bagong Tree Entry tuwing magse-save ng object.  Posible pa ring manu-manong gamitin ang mga Rule."

#: include/global_settings.php:573
msgid "Automation Notification To Email"
msgstr "Email ng Automation Notification Para Kay"

#: include/global_settings.php:574
msgid "The Email Address to send Automation Notification Emails to if not specified at the Automation Network level.  If either this field, or the Automation Network value are left blank, Cacti will use the Primary Cacti Admins Email account."
msgstr "Ang Email Address na pagpapadalhan ng mga Automation Notification Email kung hindi tinukoy sa antas ng Automation Network.  Kung blangko ang field na ito, o ang halaga ng Automation Network, gagamitin ng Cacti ang Email account ng Pangunahing Cacti Admin."

#: include/global_settings.php:580
msgid "Automation Notification From Name"
msgstr "Pangalan ng Nagpadala ng Automation Notification"

#: include/global_settings.php:581
msgid "The Email Name to use for Automation Notification Emails to if not specified at the Automation Network level.  If either this field, or the Automation Network value are left blank, Cacti will use the system default From Name."
msgstr "Ang Email Name na gagamitin para sa mga Automation Notification Email kung hindi tinukoy sa antas ng Automation Network.  Kung blangko ang field na ito, o ang halaga ng Automation Network, gagamitin ng Cacti ang default na From Name ng system."

#: include/global_settings.php:588
msgid "Automation Notification From Email"
msgstr "Email ng Nagpadala ng Automation Notification"

#: include/global_settings.php:589
msgid "The Email Address to use for Automation Notification Emails to if not specified at the Automation Network level.  If either this field, or the Automation Network value are left blank, Cacti will use the system default From Email Address."
msgstr "Ang Email Address na gagamitin para sa mga Automation Notification Email kung hindi tinukoy sa antas ng Automation Network.  Kung blangko ang field na ito, o ang halaga ng Automation Network, gagamitin ng Cacti ang default na From Email Address ng system."

#: include/global_settings.php:595
msgid "Graph Template Defaults"
msgstr "Mga Default ng Graph Template"

#: include/global_settings.php:601
msgid "Graph Template Test Data Source"
msgstr "Test Data Source ng Graph Template"

#: include/global_settings.php:602
msgid "Check this checkbox if you wish to test the Data Sources prior to their creation for new and newly imported Graph Templates.  With Test Data Sources enabled, if the Data Source does not return valid data, the Graph will not be created.  This setting is important if you wish to have a more generic Device Template that can include more Graph Templates that can be selectively applied depending on the characteristics of the Device itself.  Note: If you have a long running script as a Data Source, the time to create Graphs will be increased."
msgstr "I-check ang checkbox na ito kung nais mong subukan ang mga Data Source bago likhain ang mga ito para sa mga bago at bagong na-import na Graph Template.  Kapag naka-enable ang Test Data Sources, kung ang Data Source ay hindi nagbalik ng valid na data, hindi malilikha ang Graph.  Mahalaga ang setting na ito kung nais mong magkaroon ng mas generic na Device Template na maaaring magsama ng mas maraming Graph Template na maaaring piling i-apply depende sa mga katangian ng mismong Device.  Tandaan: Kung mayroon kang matagal na tumatakbong script bilang Data Source, tataas ang oras ng paglikha ng mga Graph."

#: include/global_settings.php:607
msgid "The default Image Format to be used for all new Graph Templates."
msgstr "Ang default na Image Format na gagamitin para sa lahat ng bagong Graph Template."

#: include/global_settings.php:614
msgid "The default Graph Height to be used for all new Graph Templates."
msgstr "Ang default na Graph Height na gagamitin para sa lahat ng bagong Graph Template."

#: include/global_settings.php:622
msgid "The default Graph Width to be used for all new Graph Templates."
msgstr "Ang default na Graph Width na gagamitin para sa lahat ng bagong Graph Template."

#: include/global_settings.php:631
msgid "General Defaults"
msgstr "Mga Pangkalahatang Default"

#: include/global_settings.php:637
msgid "The default Device Template used on all new Devices."
msgstr "Ang default na Device Template na ginagamit sa lahat ng bagong Device."

#: include/global_settings.php:645
msgid "The default Site for all new Devices."
msgstr "Ang default na Site para sa lahat ng bagong Device."

#: include/global_settings.php:653
msgid "The default Poller for all new Devices."
msgstr "Ang default na Poller para sa lahat ng bagong Device."

#: include/global_settings.php:660
msgid "Device Threads"
msgstr "Mga Device Thread"

#: include/global_settings.php:661
msgid "The default number of Device Threads.  This is only applicable when using the Spine Data Collector."
msgstr "Ang default na bilang ng mga Device Thread.  Naaangkop lamang ito kapag gumagamit ng Spine Data Collector."

