#: index.php:89
msgid "<strong>NOTE:</strong> You are logged into a Remote Data Collector.  When <b>'online'</b>, you will be able to view and control much of the Main Cacti Web Site just as if you were logged into it.  Also, it's important to note that Remote Data Collectors are required to use the Cacti's Performance Boosting Services <b>'On Demand Updating'</b> feature, and we always recommend using Spine.  When the Remote Data Collector is <b>'offline'</b>, the Remote Data Collectors Web Site will contain much less information.  However, it will cache all updates until the Main Cacti Database and Web Server are reachable.  Then it will dump it's Boost table output back to the Main Cacti Database for updating."
msgstr "<strong>TANDAAN:</strong> Naka-login ka sa isang Remote Data Collector.  Kapag <b>'online'</b>, makikita at makokontrol mo ang karamihan ng Main Cacti Web Site na parang naka-login ka mismo dito.  Mahalaga ring tandaan na kailangang gamitin ng mga Remote Data Collector ang feature na <b>'On Demand Updating'</b> ng Performance Boosting Services ng Cacti, at lagi naming inirerekomenda ang paggamit ng Spine.  Kapag <b>'offline'</b> ang Remote Data Collector, mas kaunting impormasyon ang makikita sa Web Site ng Remote Data Collector.  Gayunpaman, ika-cache nito ang lahat ng update hanggang maabot ang Main Cacti Database at Web Server.  Pagkatapos, ibabalik nito ang output ng Boost table nito sa Main Cacti Database para sa pag-update."

#: index.php:94
msgid "<strong>NOTE:</strong> None of the Core Cacti Plugins, to date, have been re-designed to work with Remote Data Collectors.  Therefore, Plugins such as MacTrack, and HMIB, which require direct access to devices will not work with Remote Data Collectors at this time.  However, plugins such as Thold will work so long as the Remote Data Collector is in <b>'online'</b> mode."
msgstr "<strong>TANDAAN:</strong> Wala pa sa mga Core Cacti Plugin, sa ngayon, ang muling dinisenyo upang gumana sa mga Remote Data Collector.  Samakatuwid, ang mga Plugin gaya ng MacTrack, at HMIB, na nangangailangan ng direktang access sa mga device ay hindi gagana sa mga Remote Data Collector sa ngayon.  Gayunpaman, gagana ang mga plugin gaya ng Thold basta nasa <b>'online'</b> mode ang Remote Data Collector."

